所以请务必看到最后，不要错过任何重要话题，因为我们不会只在项目就结束。
So make sure you stick around till the end and don't miss out on any important topic because we are not going to stop at project.

18
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:58,800
我们还将涵盖一些你绝对不能错过的重要面试问题。
We will also cover important interview questions that you can't miss on.

19
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:04,400
所以让我们开始吧，学习如何将原始数据转化为有意义的见解和智能决策。
So let's get started and learn how to turn raw data into meaningful insight and intelligent decision.

20
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:06,640
废话不多说，让我们开始吧。
So without any further ado, let's get started.

21
00:02:06,880 --> 00:02:08,800
那么，你究竟是如何分析数据的呢？
So, how do you actually analyze data?

22
00:02:09,070 --> 00:02:11,600
为了理解这一点，我想请大家认识一下 Alex。
To understand this, I want you guys to meet Alex.

23
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:13,200
Alex 是一名数据分析师。
Alex is a data analyst.

24
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:17,284
有一天，他的公司注意到上个月的销售额突然下降了。
One day his company noticed that the sales suddenly dropped in the last month.

25
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:18,720
没人知道原因。
Nobody knew why.

26
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:21,920
就在那时，Alex 被要求找出出了什么问题。
That's when Alex was asked to find out what went wrong.

27
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:23,760
他首先开始收集数据。
He started by collecting data.

28
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:28,640
他查看了销售报告、网站活动、客户评论和反馈表单。
He looked at sales reports, website activity, customer reviews, and feedback forms.

29
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:30,148
任何可能提供线索的东西。
Anything that could give clues.

30
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:33,280
在进行任何分析之前，Alex 先对数据进行了清洗。
Before doing any analysis, Alex cleaned the data.

31
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:38,240
他修正了错误，填补了缺失的信息，并确保所有内容准确无误。
He fixed mistakes, filled in missing information, and made sure everything was accurate.

32
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:41,760
干净的数据非常重要，因为错误的数据会导致错误的结果。
Clean data is important because bad data gives bad results.

33
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:45,440
接下来，Alex 对数据进行了探索，以了解发生了什么。
Next, Alex explored the data to understand what was happening.

34
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:48,320
这个步骤被称为探索性数据分析。
This step is called exploratory data analysis.

35
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:57,555
他用 Excel 进行快速检查，用 SQL 查看大型数据库，并用
Python 利用 Pandas 和 Matplotlib 等工具来组织和可视化数据。
He used Excel for quick checks, SQL to look through large databases, and Python
to organize and visualize the data using tools like pandas and matplotlib.

36
00:02:57,555 --> 00:03:00,320
在分析过程中，Alex 注意到了一些奇怪的现象。
While analyzing, Alex noticed something strange.

37
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:04,960
许多客户将商品加入购物车，但并没有完成支付。
Many customers were adding items to their cart, but not finishing the payment.

38
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:08,960
Alex 推断出可能是支付页面太慢或者让人困惑。
Alex figured out that maybe the payment page was slow or confusing.

39
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:11,588
他迅速与团队分享了这个发现。
And he quickly shared this insight with his team.

40
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:13,040
他们改进了支付页面。
They improved the payment page.

41
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:15,760
这个小的修复可能会帮助增加下个月的销售额。
This small fix could help increase sales next month.

42
00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:19,200
最后，Alex 创建了一些简单的图表和一份简短的报告。
In the end, Alex created simple charts and a short report.

43
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:21,840
他在会议上清晰地解释了他的发现。
He explained his findings clearly in a meeting.

44
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:25,760
他的工作不仅仅是看数字，而是讲述数字背后的故事。
His job wasn't just to look at numbers, it was to tell the story behind them.

45
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:29,040
Alex 使用了数据和工具这两样东西来完成所有这些工作。
Alex used two things to do all this data and tools.

46
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:33,680
最棒的是，数据无处不在，遍布在网站、APP、调查问卷等各个地方。
And the best part, data is everywhere on websites, apps, surveys, and more.

47
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:37,520
有了正确的工具，任何人都可以像 Alex 一样学会处理数据。
With the right tools, anyone can learn to work with it just like Alex.

48
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:48,480
你还需要了解一些核心概念，比如什么是让数据变整洁或混乱，如何利用统计学寻找规律，
以及如何构建他人易于理解的仪表板或报告。
You also need to understand some core concepts like what makes data clean or messy, how to find patterns using statistics,
and how to build dashboards or reports that others can easily understand.

49
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:54,724
别担心，即使你以前从未写过一行代码，我们也会一步步教给你所有这些内容。
And don't worry, we're going to teach you all of this step by step, even if you've never written a single line of code before.

50
00:03:55,040 --> 00:03:57,920
那么让我们从我们的第一个工具 Python 开始吧。
So let's get started with our very first tool, which is Python.

51
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:02,244
让我们从 Python 中最基础的概念——变量开始。
Let's begin with the most basic concept in Python, variables.

52
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:04,996
它们就像是用来存放信息的容器。
They're like a container that holds information.

53
00:04:05,326 --> 00:04:09,476
你可以用它来存储名字、数字，甚至更复杂的东西。
You can use it to store a name, a number, or even something more complex.

54
00:04:09,902 --> 00:04:16,260
例如，你可以写 name 等于 John，这将单词 John 作为字符串存储在名为 name 的变量中。
For example, you can write name equal to John, which stores the word John as a string in the variable called name.

55
00:04:16,654 --> 00:04:21,284
如果你写 age 等于 25，数字 25 就作为整数被存储。
If you write age equal to 25, the number 25 is stored as an integer.

56
00:04:21,613 --> 00:04:27,300
同样，如果你写 height 等于 5.4，Python 会将其理解为小数或浮点数。
And similarly, if you write height equal to 5.4, Python understands this as a decimal or a float.

57
00:04:27,726 --> 00:04:32,644
Python 真正方便的地方在于，你不需要告诉它你存储的是什么类型的数据。
What makes Python really convenient is that you don't need to tell it what kind of data you're storing.

58
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:34,564
它会自动识别出来。
It figures that out on its own.

59
00:04:34,830 --> 00:04:37,572
这让编写代码变得更加简单和快速。
This makes writing code much simpler and faster.

60
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:42,692
现在假设你不是只想存储一个数据，而是想存储一组项目。
Now let's say instead of storing just one piece of data, you want to store a group of items.

61
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:45,120
这就是我们使用所谓列表的地方。
This is where we use something called a list.

62
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:48,836
列表可以让你在单个变量中存储多个值。
A list lets you store multiple values in a single variable.

63
00:04:49,134 --> 00:04:57,092
例如，如果你在方括号内用逗号分隔信息，你可以使用从0开始的索引来访问任何值。
For example, if you write the information using commas inside a square
bracket, you can use indexing starting from 0 to access any value.

64
00:04:57,360 --> 00:05:01,680
所以如果我在括号里写 person 和 0，我将得到输出 John。
So if I write person and 0 in the brackets, I will get the output John.

65
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:05,060
同样，person 1 将给出输出 25。
Similarly, person 1 will give the output 25.

66
00:05:05,550 --> 00:05:07,876
列表也是可变的，也就是说可以更改。
Lists are also mutable or changeable.

67
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:12,160
这意味着你可以使用索引方法更新列表中的任何值。
That means you can update any value from the list using the indexing method.

68
00:05:12,400 --> 00:05:20,228
列表也很灵活，也就是说，你可以使用 追加 或 移
除 等简单命令向其中添加新项目或移除现有项目。
Lists are also flexible, that is, you can add new items to them or remove existing ones using simple commands like append or remove.

69
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:27,492
现在，有时你可能想像列表一样存储多个值，但你想确保之后没有人能更改它们。
Now sometimes you might want to store multiple values like in a list, but you want to make sure that no one can change them later.

70
00:05:27,726 --> 00:05:29,092
这就是元组派上用场的地方。
That's where tuples come in.

71
00:05:29,360 --> 00:05:33,860
元组与列表非常相似，但一旦创建，就无法修改。
A tuple is very similar to a list, but once it's created, it cannot be modified.

72
00:05:34,254 --> 00:05:42,212
例如，如果你在括号内写入用逗号分隔的值，你就创
建了一个包含两个值的元组，并且它们保持完全不变。
For instance, if you write comma-separated values inside parentheses,
you've created a tuple with two values and they stay exactly the same.

73
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:46,960
这意味着如果你尝试更改特定值，Python 将会抛出误差。
What this means is if you try to change a particular value, Python will raise an error.

74
00:05:47,214 --> 00:05:52,868
元组非常适合存储不应更改的数据，比如固定位置、电话号码或维度。
Tuples are great for storing data that shouldn't change, like a fixed location, phone numbers, or dimensions.

75
00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:54,980
接下来，让我们来聊聊字典。
Moving on, let's talk about dictionaries.

76
00:05:55,246 --> 00:06:02,916
Python 中的字典以键值对的形式存储数据，就像现实
生活中的字典一样，每个单词都有一个对应的含义。
A dictionary in Python stores data in pairs, a key and a value, just like a real life dictionary where each word has a meaning.

77
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:12,800
例如，如果你写下这段代码，那么 name、age 和
height 就是键，它们各自的值是 John、25 和 5.4。
For example, if you write this piece of code, then name, age and
height are the keys, and their respective values are John, 25 and 5.4.

78
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:21,200
你可以简单地通过使用它的名称，比如 person，并在方括号内放入键 name，这将给你返回 John。
You can get the value of any key simply by using its name like person
and inside the square brackets the key, name, which will give you John.

79
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:25,252
你也可以随时更新值或添加新的键值对。
You can also update the values or add new pairs anytime you like.

80
00:06:25,518 --> 00:06:31,200
现在让我们花点时间聊聊循环，这是任何编程语言中最强大的功能之一。
Now let's take a moment to talk about loops, which are one of the most powerful features in any programming language.

81
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:37,220
循环帮助我们多次重复一项任务，而无需反复编写相同的代码行。
Loops help us repeat a task multiple times without having to write the same line of code again and again.

82
00:06:37,520 --> 00:06:41,892
在 Python 中，我们主要使用两种类型的循环：for 循环和 while 循环。
In Python, we mainly use two types of loops, the for loop and the while loop.

83
00:06:42,222 --> 00:06:46,852
当你确切知道想要重复多少次时，for 循环就很有用。
A for loop is useful when you know exactly how many times you want to repeat something.

84
00:06:47,278 --> 00:06:54,948
例如，如果你想把 1 到 10 的数字加起来，你可以手动操作，
也可以让 Python 使用 for 循环来处理。
For example, if you want to add up the numbers from 1 to 10, you could
either do it manually or you could let Python handle it using a for loop.

85
00:06:55,310 --> 00:07:00,644
在这里，循环遍历从 1 到 10 的每个数字，并不断将其添加到名为 sum 的变量中。
Here the loop goes through each number from 1 to 10 and keeps adding it to the variable called sum.

86
00:07:01,294 --> 00:07:07,652
另一方面，当你想一直重复某件事，直到某个条件不再成立时，就使用 while 循环。
On the other hand, a while loop is used when you want to keep repeating something until a certain condition is no longer true.

87
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:10,564
假设你想只把数字加到 5 为止。
Let's say you want to add numbers only up to 5.

88
00:07:10,926 --> 00:07:15,812
你可以使用从 1 开始、并在数字大于 5 时停止的 while 循环。
You can use a while loop that starts at 1 and stops when the number becomes greater than 5.

89
00:07:16,238 --> 00:07:20,080
这让你能够轻松高效地自动化重复任务。
This allows you to automate repetitive tasks easily and efficiently.

90
00:07:20,334 --> 00:07:27,812
既然我们已经涵盖了变量、数据结构和循环，现在
让我们进入 Python 中最重要的概念之一：函数。
Now that we've covered variables, data structures, and loops, let's move
on to one of the most important concepts in Python that is functions.

91
00:07:28,494 --> 00:07:32,160
这是一段旨在执行特定任务的代码块。
This is a block of code that's designed to do one specific task.

92
00:07:32,334 --> 00:07:39,520
与其一遍又一遍地重复编写相同的代码，你只需要在函数内部写一次，
然后在需要的时候调用这个函数即可。
Instead of writing the same code again and again, you can just write it
once inside a function and then use that function whenever you need it.

93
00:07:40,014 --> 00:07:42,416
假设你经常需要把两个数字相加。
Let's say you often need to add two numbers together.

94
00:07:42,816 --> 00:07:47,376
你可以每次都写一遍加法逻辑，也可以创建一个函数来帮你完成。
You could write the addition logic each time, or you could create a function that does it for you.

95
00:07:47,776 --> 00:07:54,976
在这个例子中，我们定义了一个名为 addNumbers 的
函数，它接收两个输入 A 和 B，并返回它们的和。
In this example, we've defined a function called addNumbers that takes two inputs, A and B, and return their sum.

96
00:07:55,536 --> 00:07:59,296
一旦这个函数创建好，你只需调用它就可以随时使用。
Once this function is created, you can use it anytime just by calling it.

97
00:08:00,016 --> 00:08:03,748
到此为止，你已经掌握了 Python 基础知识的坚实基础。
And with that, you now have a solid foundation in the basics of Python.

98
00:08:04,110 --> 00:08:07,972
当你继续学习数据分析时，这些概念会不断出现。
These concepts will keep showing up as you move forward to data analytics.

99
00:08:08,416 --> 00:08:12,100
所以，你可以随时暂停一下，自己动手试几个例子。
So feel free to pause here and try a few of these examples on your own.

100
00:08:12,494 --> 00:08:16,176
接下来，我们将看看 NumPy，它被称为数值 Python。
