03:20:43,472 --> 03:20:51,472
例如，邮件是真实的还是垃圾邮件，交易是否为欺诈，还有很多其他的例子。
For example, whether the mail is genuine or spam, whether the transaction is fraudulent or not, and there are multiple other examples.

2677
03:20:51,854 --> 03:20:58,276
假设你住在一个封闭式住宅小区，你的小区为不同类型的垃圾设有专门的垃圾桶。
So let's say you live in a gated housing society and your society has separate dust bins for different types of waste.

2678
03:20:58,734 --> 03:21:03,712
比如一个放纸类垃圾，一个放金属类垃圾，一个放塑料类垃圾，以此类推。
So one dust bin for paper waste, one for metal waste, one for plastic waste, and so on.

2679
03:21:03,952 --> 03:21:09,348
那么你现在基本上就是在把垃圾分类到不同的类别中。
So now what you are basically doing over here is classifying the waste into different categories.

2680
03:21:09,678 --> 03:21:15,632
所以分类就是给特定项目分配一个类别标签的过程。
So the classification is the process of assigning a class label to a particular item.

2681
03:21:15,854 --> 03:21:22,788
在这个例子中，我们给不同类型的垃圾分配纸张、金属、塑料等标签。
And in this example, we are assigning the labels paper, metal, plastic, and so on to different types of waste.

2682
03:21:23,470 --> 03:21:30,432
分类算法中有一点需要注意，就是输出变量本质上是类别型的。
And one thing to note in classification algorithms is that the output variable is categorical in nature.

2683
03:21:30,830 --> 03:21:33,072
让我们拿这个例子来更好地理解一下。
Let's take this example to understand it better.

2684
03:21:33,422 --> 03:21:36,900
这里我们有学生的性别和学生的成绩。
So over here we have gender of the student and result of the student.

2685
03:21:37,152 --> 03:21:44,672
这里，性别是输入变量或自变量，而成绩是输出变量或因变量。
Here, gender is the input variable or the independent variable, and result is the output variable or the dependent variable.

2686
03:21:44,974 --> 03:21:48,352
所以我们可以看到，我们的输出变量本质上是类别型的。
So we see that our output variable is categorical in nature.

2687
03:21:48,512 --> 03:21:52,644
也就是说，它有两个类别，要么通过，要么没通过。
That is, it has two categories, either pass or fail.

2688
03:21:53,006 --> 03:21:59,492
这里我们是根据学生的性别来判断学生是否能通过考试。
And here we are trying to determine whether the student will pass the exam or not on the basis of the gender of the student.

2689
03:22:00,014 --> 03:22:07,588
所以有很多不同的分类算法，比如决策树、随机森林、朴素贝叶斯和支持向量机等。
So there are different classification algorithms, such as decision tree,
random forest, naive base, and support vector machine to name a few.

2690
03:22:08,270 --> 03:22:11,236
那么让我们简要了解一下决策树的概念。
So let's go through the concept of decision tree briefly.

2691
03:22:11,790 --> 03:22:16,772
决策树正如其名，是机器学习中的一种基于树的分类器。
Decision tree, as the name states, is a tree-based classifier in machine learning.

2692
03:22:17,102 --> 03:22:24,112
你可以把它看作一棵倒置的树，每个节点根据特定条件分割成子节点。
You can consider it to be an upside-down tree where each node splits into its children based on a condition.

2693
03:22:24,494 --> 03:22:27,652
让我们拿这个例子来更好地理解决策树。
So let's take this example to understand decision tree better.

2694
03:22:28,014 --> 03:22:32,992
这里我们正在构建一棵决策树，来找出这个人是否健康。
Here we are building a decision tree to find out if the person is fit or not.

2695
03:22:33,230 --> 03:22:40,292
根据一系列测试条件，我们最终到达叶节点，并将该人分类为健康或不健康。
And based on a series of test conditions, we finally arrive at the leaf nodes and classify the person to be fit or not.

2696
03:22:40,878 --> 03:22:44,420
接下来另一种监督学习算法是回归。
So the next type of supervised learning algorithm is regression.

2697
03:22:44,814 --> 03:22:50,980
说到回归，输出变量或因变量是连续数值。
So when it comes to regression, the output variable or the dependent variable is a continuous numerical.

2698
03:22:51,438 --> 03:22:53,252
让我们看这里的这张图。
So let's take this graph over here.

2699
03:22:53,582 --> 03:22:58,692
这里 y轴是马力，x 轴是每加仑行驶英里数。
Here we have horsepower on the y-axis and miles per gallon on the x axis.

2700
03:22:58,990 --> 03:23:05,232
换句话说，马力是因变量，每加仑行驶英里数是自变量。
Or in other words, horsepower is the dependent variable and miles per gallon is the independent variable.

2701
03:23:05,582 --> 03:23:08,804
所以我们可以看到，我们的输出变量是连续数值。
So we see that our output variable is a continuous numerical.

2702
03:23:09,006 --> 03:23:14,884
这里我们是想确定汽车的马力如何随其 MPG 变化。
And here we are trying to determine how does the horsepower of the car vary with its MPG.

2703
03:23:15,182 --> 03:23:17,540
这就是回归的概念。
So this is the concept of regression.

2704
03:23:18,414 --> 03:23:21,312
现在让我们看看监督学习的一些应用案例。
Now let's see some of the use cases of supervised learning.

2705
03:23:21,486 --> 03:23:23,716
首先是垃圾邮件分类器。
So first we have spam classifier.

2706
03:23:24,046 --> 03:23:27,952
你认为你的邮件是如何被分类为是否是垃圾邮件的呢？
So how do you think your mail is being classified as whether it is spam or not?

2707
03:23:28,206 --> 03:23:32,272
这种垃圾邮件检测基本上是基于过滤器的概念。
So this spam detection basically works on the concept of filters.

2708
03:23:32,590 --> 03:23:37,232
主要有两种类型的过滤器：文本过滤器和客户端过滤器。
So mainly there are two types of filters text filter and client filter.

2709
03:23:37,550 --> 03:23:44,964
文本过滤器通过使用算法来检测垃圾邮件中经常使用的词汇和短语。
The text filter works by using algorithm that detects which words and phrases are often used in the spam email.

2710
03:23:45,294 --> 03:23:53,252
所以像“中奖”或“你赢了”或“免费比特币”之类的短语，通常会直接触发过滤器的删除标记。
So phrases like lottery or you won or free Bitcoin are often an immediate flag for removal by filters.

2711
03:23:53,710 --> 03:23:55,556
接下来是客户端过滤。
So next is the client filter.

2712
03:23:55,886 --> 03:24:03,652
顾名思义，客户端过滤通过识别客户端身份和历史记录，来拦截恶意且烦人的垃圾邮件。
As the name states, client filter understands the client identity and history to block malicious and annoying spam email.

2713
03:24:03,982 --> 03:24:05,860
那么这个客户端过滤是怎么工作的呢？
So how does this client filter work?

2714
03:24:06,126 --> 03:24:10,912
嗯，这是通过查看特定用户发送出的所有消息来完成的。
Well, this is done by looking at all the messages of a certain user which he has sent out.

2715
03:24:11,182 --> 03:24:22,148
所以如果一个用户持续发送大量邮件，或者该用户的几条消息已经被标记为垃圾邮件，
那么在这种情况下，他们的邮件将被完全拦截。
So if a user has sent out huge amount of emails constantly or several of the user's messages have already been marked as spam,
then in that case their email will be blocked entirely.

2716
03:24:22,542 --> 03:24:24,592
这就引出了黑名单的使用。
So this brings us the use of blacklist.

2717
03:24:24,686 --> 03:24:27,952
所以垃圾邮件过滤器还包括所谓的黑名单。
So spam filters also include something known as blacklist.

2718
03:24:28,206 --> 03:24:33,380
黑名单是指将已知的垃圾邮件发送者的电子邮件地址添加到列表中的过程。
So blacklisting is the process of adding known email addresses of a spammer to a list.

2719
03:24:33,632 --> 03:24:38,404
这个列表可以防止用户的消息被转发给其他人。
And this list prevents the user's messages to be forwarded to someone else.

2720
03:24:39,086 --> 03:24:42,656
现在让我们看看下一个用例：指纹分析。
Now let's look at the next use case fingerprint analysis.

2721
03:24:42,958 --> 03:24:47,588
在指纹分析中，你会把自己的指纹作为记录保存在机器里。
So in fingerprint analysis, you save your fingerprint in a machine as a record.

2722
03:24:47,854 --> 03:24:53,348
机器会检查数据，并验证这些数据是否属于你。
So the machine checks the data and verifies whether the data belongs to you or not.

2723
03:24:53,710 --> 03:25:01,856
一旦数据保存在机器中，从下次开始，每当你把指
纹按在机器上时，机器就会扫描所有的用户数据。
So once the data is saved into the machine, from next time, whenever you put your fingerprint on the machine,
the machine will scan through all of its user data.

2724
03:25:02,126 --> 03:25:08,228
如果机器在数据中找到了你的指纹匹配项，那么你的指纹就会通过验证。
And if the machine finds a match of your fingerprint in its data, then your fingerprint will be verified.

2725
03:25:08,846 --> 03:25:15,428
既然我们已经完成了不同类型的监督学习算法，现在让我们来看看什么是无监督学习。
Now that we've completed the different types of supervised learning
algorithms, let's go ahead and understand what is unsupervised learning.

2726
03:25:15,790 --> 03:25:22,148
说到无监督学习，输入数据没有任何关联的标签。
So when it comes to unsupervised learning, the input data doesn't have any labels associated with it.

2727
03:25:22,478 --> 03:25:31,136
机器通过理解数据的底层结构来识别相似的模式，而性质相似的数据会被归为一组。
The machine understands the underlying structure of the data to identify
similar patterns and the data which is similar in nature is grouped together.

2728
03:25:31,342 --> 03:25:39,616
所以在这里，即使没有标签，机器也能理解所有的苹果在性质上是相似的，因此它们被归为一组。
So here, even though there are no labels, the machine understands that
all the apples are similar in nature and thus they are grouped together.

2729
03:25:39,854 --> 03:25:42,896
香蕉和橙子也是同样的情况。
And same is the case with bananas and oranges.

2730
03:25:43,150 --> 03:25:46,148
这就是无监督学习的概念。
So this is the concept of unsupervised learning.

2731
03:25:46,766 --> 03:25:50,756
现在让我们来看看一种叫做 K-means聚类的无监督机器学习算法。
Now let's go through an unsupervised machine learning algorithm called as k-means.

2732
03:25:51,056 --> 03:25:55,456
K-means 的目标是将相似的数据点归入同一个簇中。
So the aim of k-means is to group similar data points into a single cluster.

2733
03:25:55,726 --> 03:26:00,804
也就是说，必须具备高的簇内相似度和低的簇间相似度。
So there must be high intra-cluster similarity and low intercluster similarity.

2734
03:26:01,166 --> 03:26:11,748
也就是说，一个簇内的所有数据点应该尽可能相似，
而两个不同簇之间的所有数据点应该尽可能不相似。
That is, all the data points within a cluster should be as similar as possible and all
the data points between two different clusters should be as dissimilar as possible.

2735
03:26:12,174 --> 03:26:18,436
换句话说，簇 A 内部的所有点彼此之间应该非常相似。
Or in other words, all the points inside cluster A should be very similar to each other.

2736
03:26:18,702 --> 03:26:24,932
但当我们把簇 B 的一个点与簇 C 的一个点进行比较时，它们彼此之间就会非常不相似。
But when we compare a point from cluster B with a point from cluster C, then they would be very dissimilar to each other.

2737
03:26:25,358 --> 03:26:29,412
在 K-means聚类中，K 代表要形成的簇的数量。
And in K means clustering, K denotes the number of clusters to be formed.

2738
03:26:29,742 --> 03:26:34,692
所以在这一张图中，K 的值是 3，因此形成了 3 个簇。
So in this picture over here, the value of K is 3 and hence 3 clusters are formed.

2739
03:26:35,310 --> 03:26:37,892
现在让我们来看看一个无监督学习的用例。
Now let's go through a use case of unsupervised learning.

2740
03:26:38,414 --> 03:26:42,948
所以 Netflix 的推荐系统是无监督学习的一个完美案例。
So Netflix recommendation is a perfect use case of unsupervised learning.

2741
03:26:43,406 --> 03:26:49,796
也就是说，你在 Netflix 上观看的电视节目中，有 80% 以上是通过平台的推荐系统发现的。
So more than 80% of the TV shows that you watch on Netflix are discovered through the platform's recommendation system.

2742
03:26:50,190 --> 03:26:57,700
这意味着，你在 Netflix 上观看的大部分内容，都是由一个神秘的黑盒算法做出的决策结果。
It means the majority of what you watch on Netflix is the result of decisions made by a mysterious black box of an algorithm.

2743
03:26:58,190 --> 03:27:00,336
那么，让我简单介绍一下它的工作原理。
So let me just give you a brief of how it works.

2744
03:27:00,590 --> 03:27:07,428
Netflix 使用机器学习算法来为你推荐一些你最初可能不会选择的电影和节目列表。
Well, Netflix uses machine learning algorithm to recommend you a list of movies and shows that you might not have initially chosen.

2745
03:27:07,758 --> 03:27:14,308
为了做到这一点，它会查看内容中的细微线索，而不是仅仅依靠宽泛的类别来做出预测。
To do this, it looks through a thread within the content rather than relying on broad genres to make a prediction.

2746
03:27:14,638 --> 03:27:22,660
这就解释了为什么在观看 Marvel 节目的观众中，有 1/8
的人是第一次在 Netflix 上接触到基于漫画的内容。
This explains how 1 in 8 people who watch Marvel shows are completely new to comic book-based stuff on Netflix.

2747
03:27:23,438 --> 03:27:25,536
最后，还有强化学习。
And finally, there's reinforcement learning.

2748
03:27:25,902 --> 03:27:31,056
在强化学习中，算法通过奖励和惩罚系统来进行学习。
So in reinforcement learning, the algorithm learns through a system of rewards and punishment.

2749
03:27:31,374 --> 03:27:34,276
这里的目标是最大化总奖励。
And the goal here is to maximize the total reward.

2750
03:27:34,638 --> 03:27:37,668
让我们通过这个例子来理解强化学习。
Let's take this example to understand reinforcement learning.

2751
03:27:38,158 --> 03:27:44,196
这里我们有一辆自动驾驶汽车，它应该在不撞到任何路障的情况下到达目的地。
So here we have a self-driving car which is supposed to reach its destination without hitting any barricades.

2752
03:27:44,654 --> 03:27:49,764
在这里，自动驾驶汽车是智能体，而道路就是环境。
So here, the self-driving car is the agent and the road is the environment.

2753
03:27:50,254 --> 03:27:53,124
这里汽车采取了一个动作，直接向前行驶。
Here the car takes an action and goes straight.

2754
03:27:53,454 --> 03:27:56,772
但是当它向前行驶时，它直接撞上了路障。
But when it goes straight, it directly hits the barricade.

2755
03:27:57,006 --> 03:28:00,676
既然汽车采取了错误的动作，它就会受到惩罚。
Now since the car has taken a wrong action, it will be punished.

2756
03:28:01,070 --> 03:28:06,016
于是汽车意识到向前走是错误的，它必须向右转。
So the car realizes that going straight is wrong and it has to go right.

2757
03:28:06,318 --> 03:28:08,896
当它向右转时，它就会获得奖励。
So when it goes right, it will be given a reward.

2758
03:28:09,134 --> 03:28:15,296
这个过程不断持续，汽车就学会了如何在不撞到任何路障的情况下自己驾驶。
So this process continues and the car learns how to drive by itself without hitting any barricades.

2759
03:28:15,662 --> 03:28:20,132
所以强化学习最明显的应用就是自动驾驶汽车。
So the obvious application of reinforcement learning is a self-driving car.

2760
03:28:20,366 --> 03:28:25,956
最近的一项研究表明，超过 90% 的道路事故是由人为误差造成的。
A recent study has shown that over 90% of road accidents are caused by human error.

2761
03:28:26,382 --> 03:28:27,856
所以说，犯错是人的本能。
So to err is human.

2762
03:28:28,046 --> 03:28:31,620
但在驾驶过程中，错误往往会导致更严重的后果。
But behind the wheel, mistakes are often more catastrophic.

2763
03:28:31,918 --> 03:28:36,096
事故导致了大量不必要的死亡。
Accidents have led to a massive amount of unnecessary deaths.

2764
03:28:36,398 --> 03:28:38,736
这就是自动驾驶汽车派上用场的地方。
So this is where self-driving cars come into the picture.

2765
03:28:38,896 --> 03:28:44,708
相信我，自动驾驶汽车比人工驾驶的汽车要安全得多。
So trust me, the autonomous car or the self-driving car is much safer than a human-driven car.

2766
03:28:44,976 --> 03:28:48,868
它们不会受到人类疲劳或疾病等因素的影响。
They are unaffected by factors like human fatigue or illness.

2767
03:28:49,216 --> 03:28:51,268
这使得它们非常安全。
And this makes them very safe.

2768
03:28:51,694 --> 03:28:58,176
而且自动驾驶汽车始终保持警觉，观察周围环境并扫描多个方向。
And self driving cars are always attentive, observing their environment and scanning multiple directions.

2769
03:28:58,446 --> 03:29:02,276
汽车很难做出它没有预判到的动作。
It would be difficult to make a move that the car is not anticipating.

2770
03:29:02,670 --> 03:29:04,656
那么，自动驾驶汽车是怎么工作的呢？
So, how does a self driving car work?

2771
03:29:05,166 --> 03:29:12,864
嗯，自动驾驶汽车主要依赖三种技术：IoT传感器、IoT连接和软件算法。
Well, self-driving cars mainly rely on three technologies: IoT sensors, IoT connectivity, and software algorithm.

2772
03:29:13,024 --> 03:29:16,676
自动驾驶汽车可以使用多种类型的传感器。
There are many types of sensors available for a self-driving car.

2773
03:29:16,864 --> 03:29:23,184
例如，用于盲点监测、前向碰撞预警、雷达等等的传感器。
For example, sensors for blind spot monitoring, forward collision warning, radar, and so on.

2774
03:29:23,502 --> 03:29:28,676
所以所有这些IoT传感器共同协作，帮助自动驾驶汽车进行导航。
So all of these IoT sensors work together to help in navigation of the self-driving car.

2775
03:29:29,198 --> 03:29:31,300
接下来是IoT连接。
Next is the IoT connectivity.

2776
03:29:31,758 --> 03:29:38,544
自动驾驶汽车利用云计算来处理交通数据、天气、地图、相邻车辆等信息。
Self-driving cars use cloud computing to act upon traffic data, weather, maps, adjacent cars, and so on.

2777
03:29:38,798 --> 03:29:42,864
这有助于汽车更好地监控周围环境并做出明智的决策。
This helps the car to monitor its surroundings better and make informed decisions.

2778
03:29:43,246 --> 03:29:45,124
接下来是软件算法。
And next is the software algorithm.

2779
03:29:45,518 --> 03:29:50,468
汽车收集到的所有数据都需要经过分析，以确定最佳行动方案。
All the data which the car collects needs to be analyzed to determine the best course of action.

2780
03:29:50,830 --> 03:29:54,064
这就是核心功能，也就是控制算法。
And this is the main function or the control algorithm.

2781
03:29:54,286 --> 03:29:57,584
这就是强化学习发挥作用的地方。
And this is where reinforcement learning comes into the picture.

2782
03:29:57,934 --> 03:30:03,588
这是自动驾驶汽车最复杂的部分，因为它必须做出完美的决策。
This is the most complex part of the self-driving cars since it has to make decisions flawlessly.

2783
03:30:04,046 --> 03:30:09,264
所以，在当今世界，最著名的自动驾驶汽车是来自Tesla和Google的车型。
So in today's world, the most famous self-driving cars are those from Tesla and Google.

2784
03:30:09,646 --> 03:30:16,228
Tesla汽车的工作原理是利用被称为Autopilot的软件系统来分析其环境。
So Tesla cars work by analyzing their environment by using a software system known as Autopilot.

2785
03:30:16,590 --> 03:30:22,144
Autopilot使用高科技摄像头来查看并收集环境中的数据。
So Autopilot uses high-tech cameras to view and collect data from their environment.

2786
03:30:22,446 --> 03:30:24,836
所以，这和我们用眼睛看是一样的。
